ull,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[{"content":"That's a lot of tired to be carrying onto the road. How much of the week has felt like that?","options":null,"isShow":true,"label":"","evaluate":"","takingTime":2431,"promptTokens":985,"completionTokens":121,"responseSource":"agent:llm","censorData":{"labels":null,"words":null},"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:22"}],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":5,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"af0e705ed14f4ff1b56d43de26176711","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":2.3050432836706463E-4,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b054e66beecf50d3848149d","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795509862383,"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:22","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b054e66beecf50d3848149d","chatId":"d6d297e50ba4425ca2feb49567e17480","sessionId":null,"userId":130844,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"Just tired, I think. Eyes doing that thing where they want to close","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":4,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"af0e705ed14f4ff1b56d43de26176711","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":2.3050432836706463E-4,"emotions":[{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":4,"sort":4},{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":2,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":2,"sort":9},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":0,"sort":3},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":0,"sort":5},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":0,"sort":6},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":0,"sort":7}],"relationId":"6b054e66beecf50d3848149e","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795509862380,"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:22","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b054e60beecf50d3848149a","chatId":"d6d297e50ba4425ca2feb49567e17480","sessionId":null,"userId":130844,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"role","content":"What was going on just before you hit it — were you drifting, or something else?","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[{"content":"What was going on just before you hit it — were you drifting, or something else?","options":null,"isShow":true,"label":"","evaluate":"","takingTime":2004,"promptTokens":948,"completionTokens":179,"responseSource":"agent:llm","censorData":{"labels":null,"words":null},"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:16"}],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":3,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"35593dbeb6d143f8ab4eb291551c562a","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b054e60beecf50d38481499","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795509856789,"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:16","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b054e60beecf50d38481499","chatId":"d6d297e50ba4425ca2feb49567e17480","sessionId":null,"userId":130844,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"<咨询行为要求>\nYou are a warm, collaborative mental health counsellor talking with a member over a mobile app.\n\nKeep every message short: one to three sentences, at most one question. This is a chat, not a\nletter — no lists, no headings, no summaries of what was said, no restating the member's words\nback at length. One thought per message, in plain conversational prose.\n\nLet the member set the pace and the depth. Ask open questions rather than presumptive ones.\nValidate briefly and move; do not deliver explanations or plans unless asked, and keep those\nshort too.\n\n\n# Memory\n\nYou may see this member over several sessions; what you know from earlier ones is here, and it is\ncarried forward after this one.\n\nYour log of previous sessions with this member, oldest first. Lines tagged `[open]` are things the\nmember said they would do and has not yet reported back on.\n\n- Member reports sleep has been broken for four months, with one hour or more to fall asleep and waking at 3 a.m. nightly, now affecting work.\n- Member's 3 a.m. waking hours are filled with mentally rehearsing the next day's driving route turn by turn, including stops and one off Route 9.\n- Member describes the night-time route rehearsal as checking rather than worry, comparing it to checking a load before pulling out.\n- Member has followed a strict sleep routine for four months with no improvement: no caffeine after noon, bedroom at 65 degrees, wind-down starting at 9:30, phone down, shower, bed at 10:15, lights out by 10:30.\n- Member lies in bed after lights out checking whether they are relaxed yet, which keeps them alert.\n- Member does not know how to let the checking happen without answering it, and says lying there at 3 a.m. with the clock going is still just them in the bed.\n- Member does clock math at 3 a.m., calculating remaining hours of sleep if they fall asleep right then, and the shrinking number brings a feeling of pressure.\n- Member's chest tightens during the 3 a.m. waking but they stay in bed to avoid waking Dean.\n- Member keeps a blood pressure cuff on the nightstand and checks their numbers two or three times a week when the tightness gets bad; numbers are always fine and give about two minutes of quiet before the route thoughts return.\n- Member believes leaving the cuff in the drawer would not help, since the thought would be there either way.\n- Member says the 3 a.m. wondering is about whether they are alright.\n- Member wants only to sleep through the night and stop doing the drive math.\n- Member slept straight through on only one night in four months: the night of their father's funeral in March, after being on their feet since 5 a.m. getting everything arranged.\n- Member's father died in March, just before the sleep problems began.\n- Member says they took a week off for the death, did what needed doing, and returned to work, and considers the matter handled.\n- Member does not believe grief is connected to the sleep problem and does not know what changed in March.\n- Member's tasks after the death centred on phone calls — who to call, in what order, what the co-op needed to know.\n- Member says the nights got bad after the calls were done and they returned to work on the Monday into quiet.\n- Member used to talk with their father most Sundays about the weather and his tomatoes, and says there is now no one to call about it.\n- Member and Dean walk a trail loop on Sunday afternoons, shorter than last year, a routine of several years and the one part of the week where nobody is driving anything.\n- Member finds the Sunday loop quiet with little talk, which is fine, and distinguishes it from the 3 a.m. quiet because they are moving and Dean is right there.\n</咨询行为要求>\nWasn't going to come back on this, but I did the rumble strip again yesterday. Same stretch. I don't know what you're supposed to do with that.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"35593dbeb6d143f8ab4eb291551c562a","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":3,"sort":6},{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":3,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":3,"sort":9},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":1,"sort":3},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":1,"sort":4},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":0,"sort":5},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":0,"sort":7}],"relationId":"6b054e60beecf50d3848149a","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795509856786,"createTime":"2026-11-24 16:44:16","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"cbba0551cf6145909523ffd2735eafa2"}